      "modelAnswer": "$8 = 2^3$, so $8^{2n} = 2^{6n}$. Also $4 = 2^2$, so the numerator is $2^{6n} \\times 2^2 = 2^{6n+2}$. Dividing by $2^{6n-1}$ subtracts the indices: $2^{(6n+2)-(6n-1)} = 2^3 = 8$, as required."
